# Optional API keys for the hosted providers the chain tries before the local
# model. Copy this file to `.env` and fill in whichever you have. Leaving one
# blank simply skips that provider.
#
# You do not need any of these. With all three blank the app runs entirely on
# the local WebGPU or WASM engine, exactly as it did before hosted providers
# existed.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE DEPLOYING
# -------------------------
# Vite inlines VITE_-prefixed variables into the built JavaScript. Any key set
# here when `npm run build` runs is readable by anyone who loads the deployed
# site, and they can spend your quota. Treat this file as a convenience for
# your own machine only.
#
# For a build other people will use, leave these blank and let each person
# paste their own key into Settings, which is stored in their browser and never
# in the bundle.

# https://console.mistral.ai/api-keys — free "Experiment" mode, no card needed.
VITE_MISTRAL_API_KEY=

# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey — must be a restricted or auth key;
# unrestricted standard keys are rejected. Free-tier input may be used to
# improve Google's models, so do not point this at a private journal.
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=

# https://console.groq.com/keys — free tier, no card needed. 30 requests a
# minute and 1,000 a day, counted per organisation rather than per key.
VITE_GROQ_API_KEY=
